[ti:Patterns of Culture]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.78]Lesson 44 | 第44课
[00:02.62]Patterns of culture | 文化的模式
[00:09.88]What influences us from the moment of birth? | 从我们出生的那一刻起，是什么在影响着我们？
[00:15.46]Custom has not commonly been regarded as a subject of any great moment. | 风俗通常并没有被人们视为一个非常重要的课题。
[00:20.81]The inner workings of our own brains we feel to be uniquely worthy of investigation, | 我们觉得大脑的内部运作才是独一无二、值得研究的东西，
[00:26.82]but custom, we have a way of thinking, is behaviour at is most commonplace. | 而按照我们的某种思维方式，风俗只是最平常不过的行为。
[00:33.35]As a matter of fact, it is the other way around. | 事实上，情况恰恰相反。
[00:36.88]Traditional custom, taken the world over, | 就全世界范围来看，传统风俗
[00:39.96]is a mass of detailed behaviour more astonishing than what any one person can ever evolve in individual actions, | 是一大堆比任何个人在个人行动中演化出来的行为都更令人惊叹的细致行为，
[00:48.53]no matter how aberrant. | 无论其行为多么反常。
[00:50.73]Yet that is a rather trivial aspect of the matter. | 然而，这只是这个问题一个相当琐碎的方面。
[00:54.70]The fact of first-rate importance is the predominant role that custom plays in experience and in belief, | 头等重要的事实是风俗在经验和信仰中所起的支配作用，
[01:02.52]and the very great varieties it may manifest. | 以及它可能表现出的极其多样的形式。
[01:07.28]No man ever looks at the world with pristine eyes. | 没有人是用纯净无瑕的眼光来看世界的。
[01:11.45]He sees it edited by a definite set of customs and institutions and ways of thinking. | 他看到的世界是经过一套特定的风俗、制度和思维方式剪辑过的。
[01:18.15]Even in his philosophical probings he cannot go behind these stereotypes; | 即使在哲学探索中，他也无法摆脱这些刻板成见；
[01:23.66]his very concepts of the true and the false will still have reference to his particular traditional customs. | 他关于真与伪的概念本身仍要参照他特定的传统风俗。
[01:31.50]John Dewey has said in all seriousness that the part played by custom in shaping the behaviour of the individual, | 约翰·杜威曾非常郑重地说过，风俗在塑造个人行为方面所起的作用，
[01:39.36]as against any way in which he can affect traditional custom, | 相对于个人能影响传统风俗的任何方式而言，
[01:43.65]is as the proportion of the total vocabulary of his mother tongue | 就如同他母语的全部词汇
[01:48.64]against those words of his own baby talk that are taken up into the vernacular of his family. | 与他那些被吸收进家庭用语中的婴儿话语之间的比例。
[01:56.17]When one seriously studies the social orders that have had the opportunity to develop autonomously, | 当一个人认真研究那些有机会自主发展的社会秩序时，
[02:03.58]the figure becomes no more than an exact and matter-of-fact observation. | 这一比喻不过是精确而实事求是的观察结果罢了。
[02:09.12]The life history of the individual is first and foremost an accommodation | 个人的生活史首先是一种顺应，
[02:14.42]to the patterns and standards traditionally handed down in his community. | 去适应他所在社团传统沿袭下来的模式和标准。
[02:20.21]From the moment of his birth, | 从他出生的那一刻起，
[02:22.20]the customs into which he is born shape his experience and behaviour. | 他所诞生的风俗就塑造着他的经验和行为。
[02:27.53]By the time he can talk, he is the little creature of his culture, | 到他会说话时，他已经是其文化的小产物了，
[02:32.38]and by the time he is grown and able to take part in its activities, | 而到他长大成人、能够参与其文化活动时，
[02:37.30]its habits are his habits, its beliefs his beliefs, its impossibilities his impossibilities. | 文化的习惯就是他的习惯，文化的信仰就是他的信仰，文化的不可能就是他的不可能。
[02:45.92]Every child that is born into his group will share them with him, | 出生在他那个群体中的每个孩子都会和他共享这些，
[02:50.38]and no child born into one on the opposite side of the globe can ever achieve the thousandth part. | 而出生在地球另一端群体中的孩子连千分之一也无法企及。
[02:57.64]There is no social problem it is more incumbent upon us to understand than this of the role of custom. | 再没有比风俗的作用这一社会问题更亟待我们理解的了。
[03:05.73]Until we are intelligent as to its laws and varieties, | 在我们对风俗的规律和多样性获得充分认识之前，
[03:09.78]the main complicating facts of human life must remain unintelligible. | 人类生活中那些主要的复杂现象必然仍无法理解。
[03:15.99]The study of custom can be profitable only after certain preliminary propositions have been accepted, | 对风俗的研究只有在接受了某些前提命题之后才能有所裨益，
[03:23.68]and some of these propositions have been violently opposed. | 而其中一些命题曾遭到激烈反对。
[03:28.49]In the first place, any scientific study requires that there be no | 首先，任何科学研究都要求
[03:33.38]preferential weighting of one or another of the items in the series it selects for its consideration. | 对其选定考虑的系列项目中的任何一项都不得有偏重。
[03:40.88]In all the less controversial fields, like the study of cacti or termites or the nature of nebulae, | 在所有争议较少的领域，比如对仙人掌、白蚁或星云性质的研究中，
[03:48.21]the necessary method of study is to group the relevant material and to take note of all possible variant forms and conditions. | 必需的研究方法是把相关材料归类，并注意所有可能出现的不同形态和条件。
[03:56.75]In this way, we have learned all that we know of the laws of astronomy, or of the habits of the social insects, let us say. | 比如说，我们正是以这种方式获得了关于天体定律或社会性昆虫习性的全部知识。
[04:06.01]It is only in the study of man himself that the major social sciences | 恰恰只有在研究人类自身的领域中，各主要社会科学
[04:11.19]have substituted the study of one local variation, that of Western civilization. | 竟以对一种地方性变异——西方文明——的研究取而代之。
[04:18.21]Anthropology was by definition impossible, | 人类学按其定义而言原本是不可能存在的，
[04:21.58]as long as these distinctions between ourselves and the primitive, | 因为只要“我们与原始人、
[04:26.14]ourselves and the barbarian, ourselves and the pagan, held sway over people's minds. | 我们与野蛮人、我们与异教徒”之间的这些区分还左右着人们的头脑，它就是不可能的。
[04:32.65]It was necessary first to arrive at that degree of sophistication | 首先必须达到这样一种开化的程度，
[04:37.42]where we no longer set our own belief against our neighbour's superstition. | 即我们不再把自己的信仰与邻人的迷信对立起来。
[04:42.42]It was necessary to recognize that these institutions which are based on the same premises, let us say the supernatural, | 还必须认识到，这些基于相同前提（比如说超自然力量）的制度，
[04:51.74]must be considered together, our own among the rest. | 必须放在一起加以考察，我们自己的制度也包括在内。
